"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th. The initial budget was $500,000, later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses, and finally approved at $2M by the executive board to cover all phases. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th) and the prototype for secure file sharing, which was tested ahead of schedule. The project is moving into the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, with upcoming UI enhancements in October. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year. The team has expanded with Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing), and partnership discussions with TechInnovate for AI technology are underway."
